#: ../../technical/articles/119-error-contracts-renderers-and-record-fault-projection.md:12
msgid ""
"This chunk covers 17 core error and registry modules: 6,098 physical "
"lines, 225,797 bytes, and 46,497 measured `o200k_base` proxy tokens. I "
"read all nine assigned pages, including the complete error hierarchy, "
"output renderers, record-fault projection, and application/adapter "
"registry shards. The manifest's token count is below the 48,000-token "
"chunk ceiling. This is static inspection only: exceptions were not "
"raised, the application was not run, and no behavior or external legal "
"claim was executed or validated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/119-error-contracts-renderers-and-record-fault-projection.md:14
msgid "Registered error contracts"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/119-error-contracts-renderers-and-record-fault-projection.md:16
msgid ""
"The core layer defines seven stable categories—`ERROR`, `REFUSED`, "
"`AUTH`, `INTEGRITY`, `FAIL`, `INTERNAL`, and `LOCKED`—and a frozen, "
"strict `ErrorCode` record for code, category, message key, retryability, "
"optional public-message selection, and runbook metadata. A similarly "
"strict `ErrorEnvelope` carries the user-facing message, optional "
"precondition action, retry instruction, context, and trace ID. This makes"
" the exception taxonomy a machine-facing contract, not just a collection "
"of Python class names. Categories and metadata records "
"(`src/cadrumo/core/errors/error_codes.py`) Envelope fields "
"(`src/cadrumo/core/errors/error_codes.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/119-error-contracts-renderers-and-record-fault-projection.md:18
msgid ""
"The declared registry maps exception qualified names to those stable "
"records. It is loaded on first use, rejects duplicate code IDs and "
"duplicate class ownership, and binds subclasses created before the "
"catalogue load through a deferred set. After loading, a `CadrumoError` "
"subclass without a declaration raises an internal invariant error rather "
"than silently receiving an unstable fallback. `RecordedRegisteredError` "
"validates a recorded code through the same catalogue, allowing persisted "
"error references to be rendered without recreating the original "
"exception. Duplicate checks and lazy catalogue load "
"(`src/cadrumo/core/errors/error_codes.py`) Deferred class binding "
"(`src/cadrumo/core/errors/error_codes.py`) Registered lookup and recorded"
" codes (`src/cadrumo/core/errors/error_codes.py`) Recorded error class "
"(`src/cadrumo/core/errors/hierarchy.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/119-error-contracts-renderers-and-record-fault-projection.md:20
msgid ""
"The registry data covers authentication and profile custody, workflow and"
" wizard refusals, Modelo calculation and export boundaries, invoice and "
"ledger operations, storage and persistence failures, and adapter errors. "
"These rows declare how concrete exceptions should be classified and "
"presented; they do not themselves implement those workflows or prove that"
" every raising call site uses the intended exception. For example, the "
"catalogue classifies login-disabled and ambiguous workflow-resume "
"outcomes as non-retryable refusals, cross-bucket Modelo export as a "
"refusal, and a duplicate committed custody label as non-retryable while a"
" stale custody conflict is retryable. Auth and workflow outcomes "
"(`src/cadrumo/core/errors/registry/_application_part1.py`) Cross-bucket "
"export and custody retry distinctions "
"(`src/cadrumo/core/errors/registry/_application_part2.py`) Custody "
"duplicate-label contract "
"(`src/cadrumo/core/errors/registry/_application_part2.py`) Adapter "
"registry composition (`src/cadrumo/core/errors/registry/_adapters.py`) "
"Profile bundle journal contracts "
"(`src/cadrumo/core/errors/registry/_application_profile_bundle.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/119-error-contracts-renderers-and-record-fault-projection.md:22
msgid ""
"`retryable` has an explicit operational meaning: the identical request "
"can succeed through time or another party's progress alone; an operator "
"correction, changed argument, or different state requires a non-retryable"
" result. Category-to-process-exit mapping is also centralized: the seven "
"categories map to exit codes 1 through 7, with `INTERNAL` reserved for "
"unexpected internal faults and expected domain refusals kept outside that"
" bucket. This gives script callers consistent coarse outcomes, but the "
"static catalogue cannot show whether all callers interpret the metadata "
"correctly. Retryability contract "
"(`src/cadrumo/core/errors/error_codes.py`) Exit-code mapping "
"(`src/cadrumo/core/errors/error_codes.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/119-error-contracts-renderers-and-record-fault-projection.md:24
msgid "Rendering and exception flow"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/119-error-contracts-renderers-and-record-fault-projection.md:26
msgid ""
"`CadrumoError` is the registered root. Subclass creation binds each leaf "
"to a declared code, while a descriptor resolves codes lazily. The "
"hierarchy provides cross-layer catch surfaces such as `CoreError`, "
"`AuthError`, and `CoreNotFoundError`; the latter lets callers handle "
"resource misses consistently across layers. `SiteHealthError` transports "
"a typed structural status/evidence payload across the adapter/workflow "
"boundary without importing an adapter type into core. A narrow "
"`pydantic_validation_boundary` converts registered domain errors into the"
" builtin `ValueError` required by Pydantic and preserves the typed "
"failure as `__cause__`. Registered error construction "
"(`src/cadrumo/core/errors/hierarchy.py`) Pydantic validator bridge "
"(`src/cadrumo/core/errors/hierarchy.py`) Site-health transport "
"(`src/cadrumo/core/errors/hierarchy.py`) Shared not-found base "
"(`src/cadrumo/core/errors/not_found.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/119-error-contracts-renderers-and-record-fault-projection.md:28
msgid ""
"The output APIs construct human text or deterministic one-line JSON. JSON"
" nests the typed error under the shared success-envelope spine "
"(`schema_version`, command, active-profile label, status, notices); text "
"output adds localized category prefixes and context labels. Both use the "
"same category, code, retryability, and redacted context, while the CLI "
"boundary supplies command/profile facts and core does not scan profile "
"manifests. `build_error_envelope` also accepts a precondition action and "
"trace ID. Envelope builder (`src/cadrumo/core/errors/error_codes.py`) "
"Text renderer (`src/cadrumo/core/errors/error_codes.py`) JSON envelope "
"(`src/cadrumo/core/errors/error_codes.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/119-error-contracts-renderers-and-record-fault-projection.md:30
msgid ""
"Context handling merges string-keyed `error.context`, eligible public "
"instance attributes, and caller-supplied context, with explicit caller "
"context taking precedence. It drops private attributes and selected "
"implementation fields, removes keys classified as internal, replaces "
"values under sensitive-looking keys with a fixed redaction marker, then "
"applies `redact_for_log` to other values. Before redaction, "
"stringification permits primitives, dates/times, enums, paths, decimals, "
"and flat collections; arbitrary objects become a stable type placeholder "
"rather than a repr dump. Both text and JSON renderers pass context "
"through this path. Context merge and redaction "
"(`src/cadrumo/core/errors/error_codes.py`) Public context projection "
"(`src/cadrumo/core/errors/error_codes.py`) Safe value stringification "
"(`src/cadrumo/core/errors/error_codes.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/119-error-contracts-renderers-and-record-fault-projection.md:32
msgid ""
"`internal_record_fault_context` adds an operator-safe summary for "
"Pydantic record failures. It reports the model name, total count, up to "
"five field-path/rule pairs, and the count withheld or omitted. It never "
"copies Pydantic's `input`; unrecognized path components are replaced by "
"`<key>` unless the supplied model declares the field name. For validator-"
"authored `value_error` and `assertion_error` prose, it reports the error "
"type and raising exception class instead of the message, because that "
"prose commonly embeds the rejected taxpayer value. This gives an operator"
" a compact contract-level clue without exposing the value through the "
"public error context. The helper's usefulness depends on call sites "
"passing the relevant record class; without it, string path parts are "
"conservatively replaced. The source says the full Pydantic error payload "
"remains in the error log, so log access and retention remain a separate "
"privacy boundary. Record-fault projection and bounds "
"(`src/cadrumo/core/errors/record_fault.py`) Path and message redaction "
"rules (`src/cadrumo/core/errors/record_fault.py`) Validator-authored "
"message handling (`src/cadrumo/core/errors/record_fault.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/119-error-contracts-renderers-and-record-fault-projection.md:34
msgid "Security and implementation assessment"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/119-error-contracts-renderers-and-record-fault-projection.md:36
msgid ""
"The strongest local controls are strict/frozen error DTOs, duplicate "
"registry checks, deterministic category and retry metadata, and a shared "
"context-redaction funnel. The record-fault projector is especially "
"conservative: it drops raw input and validator-authored prose rather than"
" attempting to scrub arbitrary diagnostic sentences. `CadrumoError` also "
"keeps original exception data out of normal context merging through its "
"private-field and explicit exclusion rules. These controls govern error "
"reporting only; they do not establish authorization, network "
"restrictions, or the correctness of the underlying application "
"operations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/119-error-contracts-renderers-and-record-fault-projection.md:38
msgid ""
"There is a conditional message-disclosure risk: context values are "
"scrubbed for the envelope's `context` field, but `resolve_error_message` "
"interpolates values from the original `error.context` before rendering "
"and can fall back to raw `error.args[0]`. The "
"`public_message_from_registry` flag and canonical-key convention suppress"
" that fallback for selected codes, but ordinary registered codes can "
"still use translated text or exception text. If a template interpolates a"
" sensitive context key, or an exception constructor puts a secret/PII "
"value in its positional message, the message can expose it even when the "
"separate context entry is redacted. I found no assigned locale templates "
"or exhaustive raising call sites in this chunk to establish an actual "
"exposed value; audit those templates and constructors, and test rendered "
"text and JSON with secret-bearing contexts. Message resolution and raw "
"fallback (`src/cadrumo/core/errors/error_codes.py`) Interpolation inputs "
"(`src/cadrumo/core/errors/error_codes.py`) Separate context scrub "
"(`src/cadrumo/core/errors/error_codes.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/119-error-contracts-renderers-and-record-fault-projection.md:40
msgid ""
"The main quality strength is that classification and retry semantics are "
"explicit and centrally checked. The registry is nevertheless split across"
" numerous generated-size shards, so change review must include the "
"correct shard and the owning exception declaration. This chunk includes "
"no tests; static inspection cannot establish catalog completeness in a "
"live import, exact translation coverage, error-code stability across "
"releases, or consumer compliance with retry and exit metadata. Useful "
"follow-up is to test first-use registry loading and duplicate refusal, "
"round-trip the text/JSON envelopes, and trace Pydantic boundaries to "
"confirm sensitive record faults consistently pass through "
"`internal_record_fault_context`."
msgstr ""

